0 A long track carrier has four large wheels between small end wheels, with a spring-and-link detail at one end.
0 Name: TECHNIC_CHAIN_TREAD_38-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Wide yellow tread pads form a low, elongated loop. A row of large wheels fills the middle, while smaller wheels lift the track slightly at each end; long beams run behind them.
0 // Rigid construction: Three 32525 beams organize the carrier. 57519 and 57520 sprockets, half bushes, belt wheels and angle connectors build the wheel stack; 731/732 shock parts form the spring detail.
0 // Build lesson: Study the wheel plane, bush spacing, carrier rails and end-wheel mounting as one assembly. A clear repeated roller rhythm gives tracked industrial machinery a convincing silhouette.
0 // Reuse: The four middle sprocket placements are repeated on the return route: eight records describe four coincident wheel positions. Count each real wheel once in a new assembly; verify the spring linkage before calling it a tensioner.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
